# Interpreter-throw closure item 2 (steps/interpreter-throw-20261010.md): a NATIVE caller that declares NO throw names
# -- kept native by its C-door call -- catches the interpreter fault of its walked callee: the walked method is on the
# status channel whatever its signature declares, and the caller closes over it (before: "lmx: invariant: a callable
# that cannot throw reported a status", abort).  The sibling with a declared name: unit_walk_interpreter_native_catch.
fn: bad (int: n) int
    return: 12 / n

fn: relay (int: n) int
    int: native_probe c.abs(n)
    int: got 0
    ---
        got: bad(n)
    ---
    catch: interpreter ()
        got: 7
return: got

int: result relay(0)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: result; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
